    "engine": "jupyter",
    "markdown": "---\ngd-head-tags:\n  - >-\n    `<script type=\"application/ld+json\">[{\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\n    \"@type\": \"SoftwareSourceCode\", \"name\": \"EdgeCase\", \"description\":\n    \"High-performance graph analysis library\", \"codeRepository\":\n    \"https://github.com/rich-iannone/edgecase\", \"license\":\n    \"https://opensource.org/licenses/MIT\", \"url\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase\", \"documentation\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase\", \"programmingLanguage\": {\"@type\":\n    \"ComputerLanguage\", \"name\": \"Python\"}}, {\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\n    \"@type\": \"WebPage\", \"name\": \"Graph.is_dominating_set - EdgeCase\",\n    \"isPartOf\": {\"@type\": \"WebSite\", \"name\": \"EdgeCase\"}, \"url\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase/reference/Graph.is_dominating_set.html\"}]</script>`{=html}\nopen-graph:\n  title: >-\n    [Graph.is_dominating_set()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function .doc-label\n    .doc-label-method} | EdgeCase\n  description: Check if a set of nodes forms a dominating set.\ntwitter-card:\n  title: >-\n    [Graph.is_dominating_set()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function .doc-label\n    .doc-label-method} | EdgeCase\n  description: Check if a set of nodes forms a dominating set.\ntitle: >-\n  [Graph.is_dominating_set()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function .doc-label\n  .doc-label-method}\nbody-classes: doc-api-page doc-py-api-page\nshift-heading-level-by: 0\nbread-crumbs: false\ntoc-depth: 3\ndescription-meta: Check if a set of nodes forms a dominating set.\npage-navigation: false\nhtml-table-processing: none\n---\n\n::: {.doc-subject}\n\nCheck if a set of nodes forms a dominating set.\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-usage-source}\nUsage\n\n[Source](https://github.com/rich-iannone/edgecase/blob/main/python/edgecase/graph.py#L88584-L88687){target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"}\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-signature .doc-function}\n```pythonsignature\nGraph.is_dominating_set(nodes)\n```\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-text}\n\n![Is dominating set](../assets/graphs/is-dominating-set.light.svg){.lightbox fig-alt=\"The same two-by-three ladder on both sides, with the candidate nodes outlined. Left: every node is B, E, or next to one of them, so is_dominating_set() returns True. Right: with B and D, node F (shown in the accent color) has no neighbor in the set, so is_dominating_set() returns False.\" width=\"100%\"}\n\nA dominating set `D` of a graph `G = (V, E)` is a subset of V such that every vertex not in\n`D` is adjacent to at least one member of `D`. In other words, every node is either in `D`\nor has a neighbor in `D`.\n\nDominating sets model coverage problems where each chosen node \"serves\" itself and its\nimmediate neighbors. Use this method to check, for example, whether:\n\n- a set of facilities (hospitals, cell towers, warehouses) covers every location that\n  is one hop away\n- a set of monitors or sensors observes every node in a network\n- the output of `dominating_set()` or `minimum_weighted_dominating_set()` is valid\n\nDuplicates in `nodes=` are harmless. For directed graphs, a node outside the set counts as dominated only if it\nhas an edge pointing *to* a member of the set (an out-neighbor in `D`); edges pointing\nfrom a member to it do not count. Convert with `to_undirected()` first if you want\ndirection to be ignored.\n:::\n\n## Parameters {.doc-parameters}\n\n::: {.doc-definition-items}\n<code>[nodes]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [list[Union[int, str]]]{.doc-parameter-annotation}</code>\n\n:   The nodes (IDs or labels) forming the candidate dominating set. An empty list is\n    only a dominating set of an empty graph.\n:::\n\n## Returns {.doc-returns}\n\n::: {.doc-definition-items}\n<code> [bool]{.doc-parameter-annotation}</code>\n\n:   `True` if every node in the graph is in `nodes=` or adjacent to a node in `nodes=`,\n    `False` otherwise.\n:::\n\n## Raises {.doc-raises}\n\n::: {.doc-definition-items}\n<code> [NodeNotFoundError]{.doc-parameter-annotation}</code>\n\n:   If any of `nodes=` is not a node in the graph.\n:::\n\n## Technical Notes {.doc-technical-notes}\n\nA dominating set covers every vertex either directly or via a neighbor, so\nvalidation is a single pass: every vertex outside the input set must have at least\none neighbor inside it. The scan costs $O(V + E)$. Edge cases behave predictably:\nthe empty set dominates only the empty graph, and the entire vertex set is always a\ndominating set (trivially). A single-node set dominates exactly that node and its\nneighborhood.\n\n## See Also {.doc-see-also}\n\n[](`~dominating_set`) \n\n:   Find a dominating set quickly.\n\n[](`~minimum_weighted_dominating_set`) \n\n:   Find a small or cheap dominating set.\n\n[](`~is_vertex_cover`) \n\n:   Check that a set touches every edge instead of every node.\n\n## Examples {.doc-examples}\n\nOn a path, `B` and `D` together reach every node, but `B` alone misses `D`:\n\n::: {#a124894b .cell execution_count=1}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\nimport edgecase as ec\n\ngraph = ec.Graph.from_edges([(\"A\", \"B\"), (\"B\", \"C\"), (\"C\", \"D\")])\n\ngraph.is_dominating_set([\"B\", \"D\"]), graph.is_dominating_set([\"B\"])\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=1}\n```\n(True, False)\n```\n:::\n:::\n\n\n### Wi-Fi in every room\n\n`offices()` is the floor plan of a made-up office, with its 20 rooms joined where a door\nleads from one to the other. An access point reaches its own room and the rooms next\ndoor, so the rooms for access points must form a dominating set. One in each of the four\nhalls covers the office. Without the one in East Hall 2, five rooms on the second floor\nlose their signal:\n\n::: {#24c719df .cell execution_count=2}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\noffices = ec.offices()\nrooms = [\"West Hall 1\", \"East Hall 1\", \"West Hall 2\", \"East Hall 2\"]\nhalls = [offices.get_id_from_label(room) for room in rooms]\ncovered = set(halls[:3]) | {\n    m for n in halls[:3] for m in offices.get_neighbors(n)\n}\n\n(\n    offices.is_dominating_set(halls),\n    offices.is_dominating_set(halls[:3]),\n    [\n        offices.get_label_from_id(n)\n        for n in offices.get_node_ids() if n not in covered\n    ],\n)\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=2}\n```\n(True,\n False,\n ['Office 204', 'Lounge', 'Server Room', 'Stairs 2', 'Office 203'])\n```\n:::\n:::\n\n\n::: {#c7e37df5 .cell execution_count=3}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\noffices.plot(layout=\"pos\", highlight=halls[:3], label_by=\"label\")\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=3}\n```{=html}\n<div class=\"ec-theme\" style=\"display:contents\"><style class=\"ec-theme-vars\">:where(.ec-theme){--ect-3239c383:#fafafa;--ect-e5dfd507:#94a3b8;--ect-8a2de1d4:#374151;--ect-57425a7e:rgba(15,23,42,0.88);--ect-21ade003:#f1f5f9;--ect-61169ea5:#c2410c;--ect-63cc1385:#d4d4d8;--ect-879b7ebc:#949497;--ect-b9f8de6d:#872d08;--ect-f59ba8df:#a1a1aa}@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark){.ec-theme{--ect-3239c383:#0d1117;--ect-e5dfd507:#4b5563;--ect-8a2de1d4:#d1d5db;--ect-57425a7e:rgba(241,245,249,0.92);--ect-21ade003:#0f172a;--ect-61169ea5:#f97316;--ect-63cc1385:#3f3f46;--ect-879b7ebc:#2c2c31;--ect-b9f8de6d:#ae500f;--ect-f59ba8df:#71717a}}:is(html.quarto-light, body.quarto-light, html[data-bs-theme=\"light\"], [data-jp-theme-light=\"true\"], body.vscode-light, body.vscode-high-contrast-light, html[theme=\"light\"]) .ec-theme{--ect-3239c383:#fafafa;--ect-e5dfd507:#94a3b8;--ect-8a2de1d4:#374151;--ect-57425a7e:rgba(15,23,42,0.88);--ect-21ade003:#f1f5f9;--ect-61169ea5:#c2410c;--ect-63cc1385:#d4d4d8;--ect-879b7ebc:#949497;--ect-b9f8de6d:#872d08;--ect-f59ba8df:#a1a1aa}:is(html.quarto-dark, body.quarto-dark, html[data-bs-theme=\"dark\"], [data-jp-theme-light=\"false\"], body.vscode-dark, body.vscode-high-contrast:not(.vscode-high-contrast-light), html[theme=\"dark\"]) .ec-theme{--ect-3239c383:#0d1117;--ect-e5dfd507:#4b5563;--ect-8a2de1d4:#d1d5db;--ect